{"OrganizationCacheTest.testCacheIDPForLogin registers cleanup for identityProviders().get(\"alias\") instead of the created aliases (\"idp-alias-<n>\"), so the test leaks IDPs into the realm across test runs making the testsuite flaky and order-dependent": 0.9591543674468994, "In InfinispanIdentityProviderStorageProvider.remove, registerIDPInvalidation(storedIdp) is called even if storedIdp is null (alias not found), causing a NullPointerException when the alias key is invalidated but the provider no longer exists": 0.41864678263664246, "InfinispanIdentityProviderStorageProvider.getForLogin returns cached IDPs by internalId without re-applying the login suitability rules at return time, so it can return IDPs that became disabled due to organization/provider state changes via the organization-aware wrapper": 0.8136330246925354, "The remove() method unconditionally calls idpDelegate.getByAlias(alias) (a database query) on every invocation, even when the IDP is available in the Infinispan cache, causing unnecessary DB round-trips": 0.8681081533432007}